def countCoveredPoints(nums):
    # Since start and end are between 1 and 100 inclusive, we can use a fixed-size boolean array.
    covered = [False] * 101   # indices 0..100, we will ignore index 0 because start >= 1

    for start, end in nums:
        # Mark every integer point from start to end (both inclusive) as covered.
        for p in range(start, end + 1):
            covered[p] = True

    # Count how many positions are marked as True.
    return sum(covered)
```

